WEBVTT

00:06.170 --> 00:08.750
Tsukishima, Chuo City, Tokyo.

00:08.960 --> 00:12.420
<b>TAKAMIMI SHRINE</b>

00:09.710 --> 00:14.080
Spanning more than 400 years
since the Edo Period, is Takamimi Shrine.

00:12.420 --> 00:15.250
<b>TAKAMIMI SHRINE</b>

00:15.460 --> 00:19.790
The goddess summoned
from another world enshrined here...

00:20.420 --> 00:23.000
was an absolute social recluse of an elf.

00:23.330 --> 00:27.330
<b>Takamimi Hime-no-Mikoto - Elda</b>

00:25.210 --> 00:28.960
T-tell her the soy sauce-simmered
tsukudani was especially delicious.

00:33.250 --> 00:35.710
She said the tsukudani is especially delicious.

00:36.080 --> 00:37.580
Thank you, Elda-sama.

00:39.960 --> 00:44.880
And the bitter melon dish she made recently
was unexpected and tasty.

00:45.500 --> 00:47.830
She said the bitter melon dish was also tasty.

00:47.830 --> 00:53.880
Thank you. Oh, it's also Okinawan cuisine,
but papaya tsukudani is good, too.

00:55.460 --> 00:57.000
Uh, um...

01:00.170 --> 01:02.750
And tell her so the emotion gets across!

01:06.830 --> 01:10.420
P-Papaya?! You can make simmered FRUIT dishes?!

01:10.670 --> 01:15.380
Yes, they're much easier to eat than the bitter melon.
I'll cook some up next time.

01:16.670 --> 01:18.080
O-okay, then...

01:18.960 --> 01:22.250
Just talk to her! This is annoying and embarrassing.

01:23.210 --> 01:25.580
But if Elda-sama doesn't want to...

01:25.670 --> 01:28.420
I-I don't mind. It's not like I don't want to.

01:28.630 --> 01:32.040
It's just... it may take me some time
before I get used to this...

01:32.290 --> 01:35.630
We're talking like this so that you can get used to it.

01:35.880 --> 01:38.250
C'mon, use your words and say what you want to say.

01:38.880 --> 01:41.920
U-um... sure, okay...

01:42.170 --> 01:47.670
Koyuzu, you're great at cooking, right?
It's impressive since you're so small.

01:49.080 --> 01:50.210
Thanks.

01:50.420 --> 01:56.420
<b>Toyosu Market</b>

01:50.420 --> 01:56.420
<b>Chuo, Tokyo</b>

01:50.750 --> 01:52.750
Koyuzu cooks at the pro level.

01:53.130 --> 01:56.080
She's even acknowledged
as a connoisseur at the Toyosu market.

01:56.420 --> 02:00.670
Oh wow! What about you Koito?
Are you good at cooking?

02:01.000 --> 02:04.580
I am, you see, a fast runner. I ran track.

02:05.500 --> 02:06.540
And cooking?

02:06.920 --> 02:08.290
I'm a fast runner.

02:08.580 --> 02:09.580
What about cooking?

02:10.290 --> 02:11.710
I'm a fast runner.

02:12.130 --> 02:13.920
Koito's a robot now.

02:14.080 --> 02:15.460
I'm a fast runner.

02:16.040 --> 02:18.290
Do you like tsukudani dishes, Elda?

02:18.290 --> 02:20.000
Huh? Y-yeah...

02:20.830 --> 02:26.330
When I was first summoned to this world,
I didn't like rice very much.

02:26.920 --> 02:30.500
Even though they went to the trouble
of offering something so precious at the time...

02:31.500 --> 02:37.080
But one day, the child of the fishmonger parishioner,
well, he offered me a soy-simmered dish.

02:37.630 --> 02:42.170
It was sweet and salty and delicious!
It was like I became a rice thief!

02:42.170 --> 02:45.330
Now I can eat multiple bowls of rice!

02:45.330 --> 02:46.630
Are you a foreign wrestler?

02:47.750 --> 02:50.290
When Ieyasu-kun was building Edo,

02:50.290 --> 02:54.920
they brought in the fishermen of Tsukudamura
in Settsu Province to live around here.

02:51.130 --> 02:54.830
<b>Tsukudamura, Settsu Province Present day... Tsukuda, Nishiyodogawa Ward, Osaka City</b>

02:55.460 --> 02:57.000
I..Ieyasu-kun?

02:57.460 --> 03:02.580
Those fishermen, in order to have food on board
and non-perishable foods, made tsukudani.

03:02.830 --> 03:08.670
Basically, tsukudani is Tsukudajima,
thus it is the heart of Tsukishima!

03:08.920 --> 03:11.460
Tsukudani has transcended
the boundaries of seafood versions,

03:11.460 --> 03:13.750
and varieties such as the farm
produce and mixed ingredient type

03:13.750 --> 03:17.960
Elda-sama's ears get all twitchy when she's excited.

03:13.750 --> 03:15.920
now richly adorn the dining tables of Japanese people!

03:15.920 --> 03:17.960
It has expanded to become a standard ingredient

03:17.960 --> 03:19.540
in convenience store rice balls,

03:18.130 --> 03:21.460
I had no clue Elda had so much to say...

03:19.540 --> 03:22.920
and most Japanese people have already tried it at last once...

04:53.170 --> 04:57.790
<b>EPISODE 2</b>

04:53.170 --> 04:57.790
<b>LET'S GO TO</b>

04:53.170 --> 04:57.790
<b>MONJA STREET</b>

04:56.380 --> 05:00.420
What? Koyuzu talked with Takamimi-sama?

05:00.580 --> 05:02.670
I'm jealous. She enjoyed it, huh?

05:02.880 --> 05:07.040
Yeah, she said it was fun.
They only talked about tsukudani, though.

05:08.830 --> 05:15.500
But it's been tradition since forever that no one
besides the miko sees Takamimi-sama, right?

05:15.960 --> 05:19.630
Seems like Elda only said that
because she didn't want to see other people.

05:20.500 --> 05:22.290
Oh, good to know.

05:23.420 --> 05:25.830
But I see you're eating pretty well.

05:25.830 --> 05:30.290
Shut it! Elda is collecting the lucky combo bonus!

05:27.080 --> 05:30.880
<b>Lucky Combo</b>

05:31.830 --> 05:33.170
Frog Tanks?

05:33.380 --> 05:39.920
<b>SWIM!</b>

05:33.380 --> 05:39.920
<b>DRIVE</b>

05:33.380 --> 05:39.920
<b>FROG TANKS</b>

05:33.380 --> 05:39.920
<b>GLIDE!</b>

05:33.630 --> 05:36.500
It's like, Elda's been loving these prizes
that come with the snack lately.

05:37.750 --> 05:39.830
They're doing a collab with Wicky D's now.

05:42.130 --> 05:44.580
Huh? That's Elda's spirit magic.

05:44.960 --> 05:47.130
Miko. Oh miko...

05:47.580 --> 05:53.380
Choose the lucky combo toy #1 and #6...
I repeat, get #1 and #6.

05:53.540 --> 05:54.580
Oh, Miko...

05:54.830 --> 05:59.080
It must be hard for you, too...
Let her know I've heard her a hundred times.

06:02.790 --> 06:03.920
Thanks for the message.

06:05.330 --> 06:10.210
Anyway, Elda's paying for all this.
It's part of what a miko does.

06:11.330 --> 06:13.460
Getting chubby is getting chubby, no matter your excuse.

06:13.630 --> 06:15.420
<b>CHUBBY</b>

06:15.250 --> 06:17.500
Koma-chan is always saying stuff like that.

06:18.380 --> 06:23.210
Well... You do look cute with a little chub on you, Koito.

06:27.170 --> 06:29.960
Koma-chan is always saying stuff like that.

06:30.750 --> 06:32.790
Jeez, Koma-chan, you're so... ugh!

06:32.790 --> 06:34.080
Wh-what?!

06:41.460 --> 06:42.670
Hello!

06:43.210 --> 06:46.210
Koganei-sama, Takamimi Hime-no-mikoto-sama!

06:46.710 --> 06:48.210
I have a delivery!

06:52.670 --> 06:53.880
Stamp, please!

06:57.210 --> 06:59.250
Th-thank you for this.

07:03.920 --> 07:05.500
Thank you!

07:16.380 --> 07:19.380
<b>Frog Tanks</b>

07:16.380 --> 07:19.380
<b>3 types</b>

07:16.380 --> 07:19.380
<b>with chocolate</b>

07:23.080 --> 07:25.540
<b>Frog Panzer</b>

07:23.080 --> 07:25.540
<b>Frog Aegis</b>

07:25.750 --> 07:28.000
<b>Frog Panzer</b>

07:29.290 --> 07:32.040
The Panzer is really cool!

07:32.380 --> 07:39.330
Not buying a box with all three types of blind boxes
and daring to buy one of each is risky behavior,

07:40.130 --> 07:42.670
but I'm sure I'll get the complete set.

07:43.290 --> 07:47.790
I mean, I'm a goddess, and I'm more likely
to attract some pretty great luck...

07:48.460 --> 07:51.830
Behold! The power of Takamimi Hime-no-Mikoto!

07:52.500 --> 07:54.000
<b>TADPOLECOPTER</b>

07:55.040 --> 07:58.880
Hm, well... this is just the first one.

08:04.170 --> 08:08.000
Okay! The next one will be it! Come home, Frog Panzer!

08:09.000 --> 08:09.710
<b>TADPOLECOPTER</b>

08:09.710 --> 08:10.830
<b>TADPOLECOPTER</b>

08:18.080 --> 08:20.000
My dreams of completion have been crushed.

08:21.830 --> 08:24.290
P-please, at least one! Panzer, come to me.

08:25.790 --> 08:29.250
Come, Frog... Panzer!

08:29.250 --> 08:30.040
<b>TADPOLECOPTER</b>

08:30.040 --> 08:30.420
<b>TADPOLECOPTER</b>

08:30.420 --> 08:31.000
<b>TADPOLECOPTER</b>

08:48.420 --> 08:50.880
<b>BONSAI FROG TANKS</b>

08:48.420 --> 08:50.880
<b>vol. 3 box 8 count</b>

08:50.880 --> 08:53.830
<b>BONSAI FROG TANKS</b>

08:50.880 --> 08:53.830
<b>vol. 3 box 8 count</b>

08:56.790 --> 09:00.130
<b>Quantity</b>

08:56.790 --> 09:00.130
<b>Add to cart</b>

08:56.790 --> 09:00.130
<b>Buy now</b>

09:03.080 --> 09:05.540
<b>Frog Tanks Chocolate</b>

09:10.750 --> 09:12.170
I'm home!

09:14.790 --> 09:18.960
W-welcome back, Koito!
Wh-where's my lucky combo prize?!

09:19.460 --> 09:21.540
Yeah, yeah, I've got it.

09:24.250 --> 09:27.420
Yay! Thanks, Koito!

09:28.130 --> 09:32.000
Frog Tanks are popular, you know.
I'm so stoked I completed the set.

09:32.500 --> 09:34.290
Hey, Takamimi-sama!

09:35.580 --> 09:36.210
Huh?

09:43.250 --> 09:47.040
K-K-K-Koito! Koito! Th-th-there's a stranger here!

09:47.330 --> 09:51.000
She isn't a stranger. This is Koma Sakuraba.

09:51.580 --> 09:52.290
Yo!

09:52.790 --> 09:57.630
Y-you did it again! N-no one besides miko
can enter the inner shrine!

09:57.960 --> 09:59.880
You said Koyuzu could come in, didn't you?

10:00.000 --> 10:03.290
W-well... Koyuzu is kind...

10:03.670 --> 10:05.130
And the delivery person, too.

10:05.130 --> 10:07.750
I-it was... m-more convenient that way.

10:08.670 --> 10:11.170
Koma-chan wanted to meet you, Elda.

10:11.540 --> 10:15.500
She's my best friend that I've known since childhood,
and I can talk to her about anything.

10:16.040 --> 10:22.000
Well, I'm keeping it a secret from her that Elda
is the Lady in White I admired. It's kinda embarrassing.

10:23.460 --> 10:25.790
Say, Takamimi-sama...

10:26.330 --> 10:26.960
Huh?

10:32.460 --> 10:34.460
Your ears sure are long!

10:34.830 --> 10:37.540
Gosh! Why do you always say stuff like that?!

10:37.920 --> 10:39.920
I-I hate her.

10:40.040 --> 10:41.580
H-hey now...

10:41.750 --> 10:44.710
She's not a bad person, so just talk to her a little bit.

10:46.540 --> 10:49.420
Huh?! You're wasting money on this again?!

10:50.080 --> 10:52.580
You can't get an advance on your
monetary offerings anymore, you got that?

10:52.750 --> 10:56.290
N-no! I just bought a box online...

10:57.080 --> 11:00.790
Huh? Are monetary offerings
that much like an allowance?

11:01.130 --> 11:03.790
Yeah, I don't know about other shrines
but that's how it is here.

11:04.170 --> 11:07.960
Please, Koito, next month is the release
of the super popular theatrical anime on Blu-ray

11:07.960 --> 11:09.920
packed with ultra-special bonuses!

11:09.920 --> 11:10.920
I don't care.

11:13.330 --> 11:17.630
But the bonuses that come with snacks
nowadays sure are impressive.

11:17.790 --> 11:20.170
They look like they'd be sold normally as toys.

11:21.540 --> 11:24.040
You don't know about it either, do you, Koma-chan?

11:24.040 --> 11:27.670
Yes, the Frog Tank series is amazing!

11:28.170 --> 11:30.210
What's with that smug mug of yours?

11:33.460 --> 11:34.500
Behold, I say!

11:34.500 --> 11:38.330
It's hard to imagine this intense perspective
on the world based on this appearance!

11:38.330 --> 11:41.210
And the toy prizes are of an unbelievably nice quality!

11:41.210 --> 11:43.210
And that is Frog Tanks!

11:45.290 --> 11:47.420
Th-that was a weak response...

11:48.170 --> 11:55.290
Because we don't really get it. I mean, you love
getting extra stuff from snacks and juice, right?

11:55.290 --> 11:59.250
Y-yes, I love it. I have ever since the Edo days...

11:59.460 --> 12:01.630
What? That long ago?

12:02.290 --> 12:07.460
The medicine sold in Toyama during the Edo Period
was the first time a prize was added to merchandise.

12:07.830 --> 12:12.420
People got a type of woodblock painting
called "Toyama pictures" when they bought medicine,

12:12.420 --> 12:14.250
and I got hooked on that, too!

12:14.710 --> 12:18.540
I was so happy when I pulled my bias,
Izumo-no-Okuni-chan!

12:16.630 --> 12:18.210
<b>Izumo-no-Okuni</b>

12:18.750 --> 12:21.630
Don't talk about legendary figures
like they're a super special rare card!

12:22.830 --> 12:28.330
B-besides, Frog Tanks gives out a lot of hikifuda cards,
and you can see the seriousness of the company!

12:29.000 --> 12:30.080
Hikifuda?

12:30.880 --> 12:33.460
Th-they were advertisements in the Edo period.

12:31.750 --> 12:33.130
<b>Toothpaste</b>

12:33.830 --> 12:35.460
Customers would draw a card,

12:34.250 --> 12:40.540
<b>Face powder</b>

12:35.460 --> 12:37.080
and they were called "hikifuda."

12:37.330 --> 12:40.250
They'd be equivalent to a flier
or an official site nowadays.

12:37.330 --> 12:40.540
<b>Alcohol</b>

12:40.540 --> 12:43.000
<b>Frog Tanks</b>

12:43.000 --> 12:47.710
<b>MISSIONARY WORK</b>

12:43.000 --> 12:47.710
<b>Frog Tanks</b>

12:43.210 --> 12:46.920
And, this is Frog Tanks' official site!

12:47.710 --> 12:50.460
O-oh, I'm not really into that...

12:50.580 --> 12:55.710
Wh-why not?! On the days that limited edition goods
go on sale groups of people even stand in line all night!

12:55.960 --> 13:01.790
<b>Customers wishing to make a purchase, please line up here</b>

12:55.960 --> 13:01.790
<b>End of Line</b>

12:57.250 --> 12:58.880
Like when iPh*nes go on sale?

12:59.000 --> 13:00.710
More like when Drag*n Quest 3 came out.

13:00.830 --> 13:01.790
I have no idea about that.

13:02.580 --> 13:06.290
Hey, you're missing
a whole lot of these, huh, Elda-sama?

13:06.500 --> 13:15.830
<b>Set 1</b>

13:06.500 --> 13:15.830
<b>Frog Cannon</b>

13:06.500 --> 13:15.830
<b>Frog Base</b>

13:06.500 --> 13:15.830
<b>Frog Dome</b>

13:06.750 --> 13:08.000
Uh, yes.

13:08.250 --> 13:12.130
These are from the first set, so now they're rare items.

13:12.330 --> 13:15.250
I was late getting into Frog Tanks.

13:15.960 --> 13:17.920
They aren't being sold anywhere anymore.

13:18.170 --> 13:21.460
They pop up on auction sites sometimes,
but those come with premium prices,

13:21.460 --> 13:24.670
and negotiating with strangers is scary.

13:24.960 --> 13:27.130
Yeah, I really want them...

13:27.630 --> 13:32.580
Well, the run-down toy shop
near my house might sell these.

13:32.790 --> 13:34.460
Huh? They sell them?

13:35.040 --> 13:37.000
The Frog Cannon? R-really?!

13:37.290 --> 13:40.210
Yeah, customers don't really go there,

13:40.210 --> 13:44.630
and the old guy only runs the shop as a hobby,
so there may be some that haven't sold yet.

13:44.630 --> 13:47.330
K-Koito! B-buy it for me!

13:47.500 --> 13:48.670
What?

13:48.670 --> 13:51.210
Elda-sama, can't you go buy it yourself?

13:52.580 --> 13:55.880
B-but it's scary out there...

13:58.920 --> 14:00.880
What a waste.

14:01.330 --> 14:06.170
You're so pretty so you should
go out more and show it off!

14:09.580 --> 14:12.580
Well, everyone goes at their own pace, I guess.

14:12.960 --> 14:16.630
I'm heading out now to buy the Frog Cannon for you.

14:17.880 --> 14:21.380
And, I'll come back to see you. Sound good?

14:22.290 --> 14:23.920
Y-yeah.

14:25.250 --> 14:27.670
Thanks for having me, Elda-sama, Koito.

14:27.670 --> 14:30.000
Yeah, sure, see ya later.

14:31.630 --> 14:34.540
S-somehow Koma-chan's kind of dreamy.

14:34.960 --> 14:37.460
Koma-chan's always saying stuff like that.

14:57.710 --> 15:00.500
Was today the sale on Futaba milk?

15:00.630 --> 15:02.460
I have to buy some for my sister.

15:04.000 --> 15:05.420
Oh, Koyuzu-chan!

15:06.500 --> 15:08.500
Kijima-san, hello!

15:08.670 --> 15:13.000
Have you got a minute?
There's something I want to ask you about.

15:14.960 --> 15:15.830
Sure!

15:17.000 --> 15:19.000
Here. This is from Koma-chan.

15:17.170 --> 15:19.420
<b>Frog Tanks</b>

15:17.170 --> 15:19.420
<b>Set 1</b>

15:17.170 --> 15:19.420
<b>Frog Cannon</b>

15:19.420 --> 15:23.080
Whoa, it's the Frog Cannon! I-I'm so happy!

15:24.960 --> 15:27.130
Isn't Koma-chan coming over today?

15:28.040 --> 15:32.670
She wanted to, but she's on the planning committee
for the cultural festival, so she's busy.

15:32.880 --> 15:34.290
She said she'll come by some other time.

15:34.290 --> 15:37.460
O-okay... I wanted to thank her, though.

15:38.710 --> 15:40.290
Koma-chan also gave me this.

15:42.500 --> 15:44.380
She said since you like it so much.

15:44.830 --> 15:47.920
Wow, tsukudani! And from Suzuki-ya, no less!

15:48.130 --> 15:52.750
I think someone gave it to her, since it seems
Koma-chan's folks rarely eat tsukudani.

15:53.130 --> 15:58.960
Oh really? Well, that's a shame, what with tsukudani
being the soul food of Tsukishima and everything.

15:59.170 --> 16:04.580
What? That's an exaggeration, don't you think? When I
think of Tsukishima's soul food, I think of monjayaki.

16:04.830 --> 16:08.380
What? Tsukishima's soul food is tsukudani.

16:09.750 --> 16:10.460
Huh?

16:10.540 --> 16:11.380
Eh?

16:15.250 --> 16:18.040
I'll have to ask my sister and Elda after all.

16:18.670 --> 16:21.250
I'm telling you, Tsukishima's soul food is monjayaki!

16:22.210 --> 16:25.250
Wh-what are you talking about? It's obviously tsukudani!

16:25.380 --> 16:29.080
Ever since I was a kid,
monjayaki has been synoymous with Tsukishima!

16:29.420 --> 16:32.170
There's even a "Monja Street" on the first block!

16:32.380 --> 16:35.290
M-Monja Street? What is that?

16:35.540 --> 16:38.630
It's where the monjayaki restaurants have always been!

16:38.630 --> 16:41.540
Elda, you went down there
in the portable shrine during festivals!

16:41.670 --> 16:46.670
Huh? What?! Is that what's usually there?
So it's not only there when there's a festival?!

16:46.830 --> 16:50.630
B-but that street smells like a delicious sauce...

16:50.830 --> 16:54.080
Monja is where they put sugar
in wheat flower and they fry it up...

16:54.080 --> 16:55.790
Huh, sugar?

16:56.790 --> 17:03.130
Wh-what? The Edo monja that I know
is like a sweet snack-type of thing, though.

17:03.500 --> 17:07.210
Elda, is it possible that you've
never had monjayaki before?

17:11.750 --> 17:16.830
I-I've eaten it before! It's just that the way
you call it "monjayaki" is strange!

17:16.830 --> 17:18.920
On a hot copper plate, just for fun,

17:18.920 --> 17:21.460
we use seeds to write moji characters
and then eat them and that's why it's called "moji" yaki.

17:20.130 --> 17:21.670
<b>Mojiyaki</b>

17:21.670 --> 17:23.290
With an accent, it's "monja"!

17:22.710 --> 17:23.710
<b>Monja</b>

17:23.710 --> 17:26.830
"Monjayaki" is "Mojiyaki-yaki" isn't it?!

17:26.960 --> 17:29.750
It's evolving into "yaki-yaki"?!

17:30.170 --> 17:33.790
There are tons of different toppings nowadays!

17:33.790 --> 17:35.250
T-toppings?

17:36.250 --> 17:39.920
Like the most popular one at this shop is... look!

17:40.540 --> 17:42.330
Mochi spicy cod roe with cheese!

17:43.170 --> 17:47.040
Huh?! Mochi and spicy cod roe
and cheese has to be delicious...

17:47.670 --> 17:48.460
Huh?

17:49.960 --> 17:52.710
N-nothing at all.

17:53.540 --> 17:57.250
It IS different from the monja that I know.

17:57.830 --> 18:01.920
Whoa! This place has a new one: clam chowder monja!

18:01.920 --> 18:03.710
Even clam chowder can be monja?!

18:03.880 --> 18:05.330
E-excuse me...

18:05.540 --> 18:08.040
Oh, welcome home Koyuzu. What's up?

18:08.380 --> 18:14.880
Well, this is a really big coincidence, but just a little
while ago I was consulted about a new monja menu,

18:15.000 --> 18:17.080
by Kijima-san at the tourism association.

18:17.880 --> 18:18.710
Really?

18:18.920 --> 18:20.790
Th-that's awesome, Koyuzu!

18:22.540 --> 18:27.170
So for dinner tonight, I was thinking
it'd be nice to go do research at the monja restaurant.

18:27.540 --> 18:28.830
Sounds good!

18:29.080 --> 18:33.080
Grandpa's at a meeting today so he won't be around.
Let's go eat some monjayaki!

18:33.080 --> 18:36.790
Huh?! What?! Wh-what about my dinner?

18:38.040 --> 18:39.670
You can come with us.

18:39.960 --> 18:40.710
Huh?

18:41.040 --> 18:44.420
I... I don't like going out there.

18:44.420 --> 18:50.420
You can't go wrong with mochi, spicy cod roe, and
cheese. And bacon and egg monja, and curry monja...

18:50.830 --> 18:53.670
Oh! And let's try the clam chowder one
I mentioned earlier!

18:53.790 --> 18:54.460
Huh?

18:54.670 --> 18:56.830
Let's go, Elda-sama!

18:56.960 --> 18:58.460
B-but...

18:58.750 --> 19:04.290
You eat your meals alone, right?
I've always thought that looked lonely.

19:04.830 --> 19:08.330
So today, let's eat together.

19:08.500 --> 19:09.250
Let's eat together...

19:09.250 --> 19:10.080
Let's eat together...

19:10.080 --> 19:11.040
Let's eat together...

19:11.040 --> 19:12.170
Let's eat together...

19:14.170 --> 19:15.420
What a sweet girl!

19:16.380 --> 19:22.080
M-maybe... I can go out to eat just for today...

19:25.170 --> 19:28.080
All right. Your big sister is treating everyone today!

19:28.330 --> 19:29.420
Hooray!

19:29.580 --> 19:32.210
Th-then I want to eat sushi.

19:32.210 --> 19:34.130
We just said we're going to eat monjayaki!

19:38.960 --> 19:39.830
Good evening!

19:40.460 --> 19:42.670
<b>Monbe</b>

19:40.670 --> 19:42.290
W-welcome in!

19:42.960 --> 19:44.710
Kado-chan, we're here for dinner!

19:45.380 --> 19:48.290
Huh? There aren't any customers.

19:48.960 --> 19:51.710
It's true. It's usually so lively in here, though.

19:52.290 --> 19:57.040
All seats are reserved for today,
since Takamimi-sama is visiting.

19:57.630 --> 19:58.380
Huh?

19:58.500 --> 20:01.380
For real? You don't need to do all that for us!

20:02.130 --> 20:07.420
Well, Takamimi-sama can feel more at ease
this way, right? Now, please come this way.

20:07.830 --> 20:08.790
Okay!

20:12.130 --> 20:15.830
Now, first up is the most popular one,
mochi, spicy cod roe, and cheese monja, right?

20:18.210 --> 20:20.750
Make it! Koyuzu, make it!

20:20.750 --> 20:21.580
Right!

20:21.830 --> 20:24.630
First I put the spicy cod roe on the cheese,

20:26.130 --> 20:27.920
then make a dam with the cabbage.

20:32.670 --> 20:35.630
Then pour the broth so that it can't escape.

20:36.080 --> 20:40.750
Put in the spicy cod roe and the cheese,
and stir it until it gets viscuous.

20:43.830 --> 20:45.500
And it's all done!

20:45.710 --> 20:47.960
Whoa! Looks yummy!

20:48.920 --> 20:50.710
And smells so good.

20:51.420 --> 20:52.920
I'm digging in!

20:53.500 --> 20:54.790
Hot, hot, hot...

20:57.420 --> 20:59.880
Mmm, delicious!

21:03.710 --> 21:04.830
Good, right?

21:26.170 --> 21:27.080
You're clapping your hands in prayer?!

21:28.500 --> 21:29.710
Yummy...

21:31.960 --> 21:34.540
Monja is yummy!

21:35.130 --> 21:37.380
Kado-chan, we're ready for the next one!

21:37.540 --> 21:38.380
Coming right up!

21:39.130 --> 21:40.880
Wanna try cooking it, Elda-sama?

21:40.880 --> 21:42.420
Eh? O-okay!

21:42.880 --> 21:44.710
Elda, the dam has been breached!

21:44.710 --> 21:46.130
O-oh no!

21:46.130 --> 21:48.080
Close it up over there, Sis!

21:48.080 --> 21:50.630
Uh, like this?! Crap, I made it worse!

21:51.710 --> 21:57.790
This is fun! Eating together is fun!

22:05.710 --> 22:07.080
That was delicious.

22:07.710 --> 22:11.580
Sh-she ate enough for 10!

22:12.130 --> 22:19.460
Nice... monja is great... No matter what
you put in, it's tasty. I want to put snacks in one.

22:19.710 --> 22:20.670
Snacks?

22:21.960 --> 22:24.790
Like potato chips and other goodies...

22:25.170 --> 22:28.000
Like those corn soup snacks would be amazing!

22:25.170 --> 22:28.170
<b>Cornsantarou</b>

22:25.170 --> 22:28.170
<b>Corn soup flavor</b>

22:25.170 --> 22:28.170
<b>Salted</b>

22:28.460 --> 22:30.420
Oh! That might work!

22:30.420 --> 22:34.080
Monja for kids made with snacks!
We came up with a new menu!

22:34.080 --> 22:35.670
Thanks, Elda-sama!

22:36.290 --> 22:40.460
Yes, of course! It was delicious. Thank you, Koyuzu.

22:44.960 --> 22:46.960
This sure is a long receipt!

22:46.960 --> 22:48.580
Th-thanks for coming!

22:49.330 --> 22:54.250
Ugh... I wonder if Grandpa
will give me an advance on my allowance...

22:54.250 --> 22:57.170
Koito! Let's come back here again!
